// Typechecking for the Playwright suite.
//
// 🔴 WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `tsconfig.json` excludes `e2e` (and the unit tests),
// so nothing ever type-checked the specs. That is the root cause of the class of
// Lane A failure that has been mistaken for stale selectors for months: when a
// spec called `txnModal.accountSelect` after the page object had dropped it, the
// only symptom was `locator.click: Test timeout of 30000ms exceeded` — 30 seconds
// of waiting, then an error naming the wrong problem. Typechecked, the same rot
// surfaces in two seconds as `Property 'accountSelect' does not exist on type
// 'TransactionFormModal'`, pointing at the exact line.
//
// This config is wired into the verification gate, so the specs cannot drift out
// of sync with the page objects again without the build saying so.
//
// `lib` is raised to ES2022 (the app targets ES2020) purely so specs may use
// `Array.prototype.at`; nothing here is bundled or shipped.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["e2e"],
  "exclude": []
}
